# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: ES
# source: https://www.boe.es/buscar/act.php?id=BOE-A-2015-11430
#   (Estatuto de los Trabajadores art. 37.2, consolidated BOE text; local copy
#   papers/holidays/es_estatuto_trabajadores_art37_boe.html) for the national
#   fiesta set, and the yearly "relación de fiestas laborales" resolutions of the
#   Dirección General de Trabajo for the per-year national traslado outcomes and
#   the autonomous-community (comunidad autónoma) layer:
#     2023: BOE-A-2022-16755 (papers/holidays/es_boe_BOE-A-2022-16755.html)
#     2024: BOE-A-2023-22014 (papers/holidays/es_boe_BOE-A-2023-22014.html)
#     2025: BOE-A-2024-21316 (papers/holidays/es_boe_BOE-A-2024-21316.html)
#     2026: BOE-A-2025-21667 (papers/holidays/es_boe_BOE-A-2025-21667.html)
#
#   NATIONAL Sunday TRASLADO (deterministic). Estatuto art. 37.2: a national
#   fiesta that falls on a Sunday is moved to the following Monday. This is
#   modelled with the sun_mon observed-shift on the national fixed rules. Across
#   every BOE resolution 2023-2026 this reproduces the published "Lunes siguiente
#   a ..." national entries exactly: Año Nuevo 2023 (Sun 1 Jan -> Mon 2 Jan),
#   Inmaculada 2024 (Sun 8 Dec -> Mon 9 Dec), Fiesta Nacional 2025 (Sun 12 Oct ->
#   Mon 13 Oct), Todos los Santos + Constitución 2026 (Sun -> following day). The
#   BOE resolutions above are the citation/verification of each yearly outcome.
#   NOTE: the vacanza/holidays reference package instead DROPS a Sunday national
#   holiday; we follow the BOE (which shifts it), so those Mondays are documented
#   our-only differential entries in test_holidays_es.py (accuracy over parity).
#
#   REGIONAL layer (comunidad autónoma). Each of the 17 comunidades + Ceuta and
#   Melilla fixes its extra holidays every year by BOE resolution; these are
#   genuine annual decrees, so they are modelled with decree rows carrying the
#   exact per-year dates transcribed from the four BOE tables above (2023-2026,
#   completeness prioritised for 2024-2025). Each community's own regional-day
#   traslado is merged into that day's decree (e.g. Día de Asturias 2024 -> 9 Sep,
#   the Monday after Sunday 8 Sep). The nationwide "Lunes siguiente a [national]"
#   BOE rows are NOT duplicated here — they are the national traslado above.
#   Subdivision codes are ISO 3166-2:ES.
# retrieved: 2026-07-21
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed | valid
#
# --- national fiestas laborales (Estatuto de los Trabajadores art. 37.2) ---
fixed  | Año Nuevo                       | 1 1   | public          |  | sun_mon
fixed  | Epifanía del Señor              | 1 6   | public religious |  | sun_mon
easter | Viernes Santo                   | -2    | public religious |  |
fixed  | Fiesta del Trabajo              | 5 1   | public          |  | sun_mon
fixed  | Asunción de la Virgen           | 8 15  | public religious |  | sun_mon
fixed  | Fiesta Nacional de España       | 10 12 | public          |  | sun_mon
fixed  | Todos los Santos                | 11 1  | public religious |  | sun_mon
fixed  | Día de la Constitución Española | 12 6  | public          |  | sun_mon
fixed  | Inmaculada Concepción           | 12 8  | public religious |  | sun_mon
fixed  | Natividad del Señor             | 12 25 | public religious |  | sun_mon
